# Bring a held work-piece to a handoff pose, signal ready, and wait for release.
#
# Deliberately single-robot (ADR-0024). It takes a pose and an opaque rendezvous
# token, never a peer's identity, so a skill never knows which robot — if any —
# is on the other side. L4 owns the ownership transfer and the two-party
# confirmation; this action owns only the motion.
#
# That split is what makes a handoff testable in isolation, which is what v1's
# handoff protocol never was: it published to a topic nothing subscribed to and
# every transaction timed out forever, with no test able to notice.

geometry_msgs/PoseStamped handoff_pose
string rendezvous_token                 # issued by L4; opaque to this layer
string workpiece_id
builtin_interfaces/Duration hold_timeout  # bounded, with a defined outcome: on
                                        # expiry the piece is still held and the
                                        # result is TIMEOUT, never a silent drop
---
ResultCode result
bool still_holding                      # true after a TIMEOUT — the upstream
                                        # robot retains ownership
builtin_interfaces/Duration duration
---
uint8 PHASE_PLANNING=0
uint8 PHASE_APPROACHING=1
uint8 PHASE_WAITING_FOR_PEER=2
uint8 PHASE_RELEASING=3
uint8 PHASE_RETREATING=4
uint8 phase
builtin_interfaces/Duration waited
